(D6 — Discrepancy 6 repro: LANGUAGE.md:3786-3788 introduces the whole
 section with "see examples/initramfs.vox for a complete, working
 early-userspace init sequence exercising all of them together". The
 example exercises the directory, mount, device-node, symlink, pivot_root
 and Execute constructs. It exercises none of the rest of the section.
 Confirmed by grep over the example:
   $ grep -ci -E 'fork|reap|Send signal|Shutdown|Reboot|Halt' \
       /home/josj/scr/english/vox/examples/initramfs.vox   ->  0
 This repro is a program built only from the constructs of this same
 section that the example never uses, so "all of them together" is short
 by at least these six. It also shows they compose fine — the gap is in
 the sentence, not in the language.
 SAFETY: the fork'd child is this program's own and is reaped; Halt is
 EPERM-safe unprivileged (see PRC-78's header before running).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/D6.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the poll of a running child returned 0
   the child was reaped
   the reaped status says signal 9
   Halt set the error flag, as it must for an unprivileged process
)
a number called 'the child' is fork the process.
If 'the child' is 0 then, Wait 2 seconds, Exit 0.
a number called 'the poll' is reap child 'the child' without waiting.
print "the poll of a running child returned {'the poll'}".
Send signal 9 to process 'the child'.
a number called reaped is reap any child process.
If reaped is 'the child' then, print "the child was reaped".
print "the reaped status says signal {the reaped status bit-and 127}".
Halt.
On error print "Halt set the error flag, as it must for an unprivileged process".
